text:
It is the morning of a clear day in March,
And I am standing on my porch in Maine;
My neighbor’s cow across the way is lowing,
The blackbird sings in some old plum tree;

There is no sun to shine upon the land—
There is only sky above me and grass below—
And here are tears that I have wept tonight;
Here is the blood-red poppy on the snow.
